{
  "title": "37: al-Saaffaat الصافات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالصّٰٓفّٰتِ صَفًّا ۙ‏(1)\n\nBy those who range themselves in ranks,\nفَالزّٰجِرٰتِ زَجْرًا ۙ‏(2)\n\nAnd (by) those, who drive away the evil with reproof,\nفَالتّٰلِيٰتِ ذِكْرًا ۙ‏(3)\n\nAnd by the reciters of Qur’an,\nاِنَّ اِلٰهَكُمْ لَوَاحِدٌ ؕ‏(4)\n\nVerily your God is (only) One.\nرَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ الْمَشَارِقِ ؕ‏(5)\n\nThe Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, and the Lord of the places of the rising of (the sun and the moon).\nاِنَّا زَيَّنَّا السَّمَآءَ الدُّنْيَا بِزِيْنَةِ اۨلْكَوَاكِبِۙ‏(6)\n\nVerily We have adorned the heaven nearest to this world (earth) with an adornment, the stars,\nوَحِفْظًا مِّنْ كُلِّ شَيْطٰنٍ مَّارِدٍۚ‏(7)\n\nAnd (which is also) a guard against every rebellious Satan;\nلَّا يَسَّمَّعُوْنَ اِلَى الْمَلَاِ الْاَعْلٰى وَيُقْذَفُوْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ جَانِبٍۖ ‏(8)\n\n(So that) They may hear not (what passeth in) the assembly on high, and they are darted from every side.\nدُحُوْرًا  وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ وَّاصِبٌ  ۙ‏(9)\n\n(To be) Driven off, and for them being a perpetual chastisement,\nاِلَّا مَنْ خَطِفَ الْخَطْفَةَ فَاَتْبَعَهٗ شِهَابٌ ثَاقِبٌ‏(10)\n\nExcept, he who stealeth (a word) by stealth then pursueth him a glistening flame.\nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَهُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمْ مَّنْ خَلَقْنَاؕ اِنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ لَّازِبٍ‏(11)\n\nAsk them then (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Are they stronger in creation or (the others) whom We have made?” Verily We created them of a sticky clay.\nبَلْ عَجِبْتَ وَيَسْخَرُوْنَ‏(12)\n\nNay! Wonderest thou (at their disbelief) while they mock (at thee)\nوَاِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا لَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ‏(13)\n\nAnd when they are warned, they mind not,\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْا اٰيَةً يَّسْتَسْخِرُوْنَ‏(14)\n\nAnd when they see a sign they incite mocking (at it)\nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ ۖۚ‏(15)\n\nAnd say they: “this is but an open sorcery\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَۙ‏(16)\n\nWhat! when we are dead and are dust and bones, shall we (even then) indeed be raised?\nاَوَاٰبَآؤُنَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَؕ‏(17)\n\nAnd (also) our fathers of yore?\nقُلْ نَعَمْ وَاَنْتُمْ دٰخِرُوْنَۚ‏(18)\n\nSay thou: “Yea! ye shall be disgraced\nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ فَاِذَا هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(19)\n\nThen it will only be a single roar, when lo! they shall gaze (around),\nوَقَالُوْا يٰوَيْلَنَا هٰذَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِ‏(20)\n\nAnd they shall say: “Oh! Woe unto us! This is the Day of Reckoning;\nهٰذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(21)\n\nThis is the Day of Judgment which ye used to belie\nاُحْشُرُوا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا وَاَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(22)\n\n(And the angels will be commanded): “Gather ye together those who were unjust and their mates, and what they used to worship,\nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَاهْدُوْهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(23)\n\nBesides God, and lead them all unto Hell.\nوَقِفُوْهُمْ اِنَّهُمْ مَّسْئُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(24)\n\nAnd stop them, for verily they have to be questioned:\nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنَاصَرُوْنَ‏(25)\n\n( Saying) “How now, that ye help not one another?\nبَلْ هُمُ الْيَوْمَ مُسْتَسْلِمُوْنَ‏(26)\n\nNay! on that day they shall be submitting themselves.\nوَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(27)\n\nAnd some of them shall advance unto the others questioning each other.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَاْتُوْنَنَا عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ‏(28)\n\nThey shall say: “Verily ye did come unto us beguiling from the right side.\nقَالُوْا بَلْ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَۚ‏(29)\n\nThey shall say: “Nay! ye (yourselves) were not the believers:\nوَمَا كَانَ لَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنِۚ بَلْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا طٰغِيْنَ‏(30)\n\nAnd there was not for us over you any authority. Nay! ye were a people rebellious!\nفَحَقَّ عَلَيْنَا قَوْلُ رَبِّنَآ ۖ اِنَّا لَذَآئِقُوْنَ‏(31)\n\nSo now hath been proved true against us the sentence of Our Lord that verily we shall (have to) taste (the doom)\nفَاَغْوَيْنٰكُمْ اِنَّا كُنَّا غٰوِيْنَ‏(32)\n\nAnd we led you astray, for verily we ourselves were astray.\nفَاِنَّهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ فِى الْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُوْنَ‏(33)\n\nVerily they on that day shall be the sharers in the punishment.\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(34)\n\nVerily, thus do We deal with the guilty ones.\nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْۤا اِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُۙ يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَۙ‏(35)\n\nVerily they, when it was said unto them that there is no god but God, used to behave proudly,\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ اَئِنَّا لَتٰرِكُوْۤا اٰلِهَتِنَا لِشَاعِرٍ مَّجْنُوْنٍ ؕ‏(36)\n\nAnd (used) to say “What! Are we to indeed give up our gods for a poet (who is) crazed?\nبَلْ جَآءَ بِالْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(37)\n\nNay! he hath come with the truth and did testify the (preceding) apostles.\nاِنَّكُمْ لَذَآئِقُوا الْعَذَابِ الْاَلِيْمِۚ‏(38)\n\nVerily, ye will taste the painful chastisement.\nوَمَا تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۙ‏(39)\n\nAnd ye shall be recompensed not but what ye were doing,\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(40)\n\nSave the servants of God, the freed ones (from evil inclinations).\nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(41)\n\nThey, for them is a sustenance known,\nفَوَاكِهُۚ وَهُمْ مُّكْرَمُوْنَۙ‏(42)\n\nFruits, and they shall be highly honoured,\nفِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(43)\n\nIn the gardens bountiful,\nعَلٰى سُرُرٍ مُّتَقٰبِلِيْنَ‏(44)\n\nUpon couches facing each other\nيُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِكَاْسٍ مِّنْ مَّعِيْنٍۢ ۙ‏(45)\n\nRound will go unto them a cup from a clear spring,\nبَيْضَآءَ لَذَّةٍ لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(46)\n\nLimpid white, delicious unto those who, drink.\nلَا فِيْهَا غَوْلٌ وَّلَا هُمْ عَنْهَا يُنْزَفُوْنَ‏(47)\n\nNothing therein to oppress the sense, nor shall they be exhausted therewith\nوَعِنْدَهُمْ قٰصِرٰتُ الطَّرْفِ عِيْنٌۙ‏(48)\n\nAnd with them shall be chaste women with modest gaze, with big (beautiful) eyes,\nكَاَنَّهُنَّ بَيْضٌ مَّكْنُوْنٌ‏(49)\n\nAs if they were eggs (secured) hidden\nفَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(50)\n\nAnd shall advance some of them unto the others questioning each other.\nقَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ اِنِّىْ كَانَ لِىْ قَرِيْنٌۙ‏(51)\n\nShall say a speaker (among them) who shall speak: “Verily, there was of mine an intimate one,\nيَقُوْلُ اَءِ نَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُصَدِّقِيْنَ‏(52)\n\nHe used to say: “What! art thou (too, indeed) of the testifying ones (of the Resurrection)?\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَدِيْنُوْنَ‏(53)\n\nWhat! when we are dead and are dust and bones, shall we (even) then in fact be brought to account?\nقَالَ هَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّطَّلِعُوْنَ‏(54)\n\nHe shall say (unto those around him): “Will ye look?\nفَاطَّلَعَ فَرَاٰهُ فِىْ سَوَآءِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(55)\n\nThen he looked down and saw him in the midst of Hell.\nقَالَ تَاللّٰهِ اِنْ كِدْتَّ لَتُرْدِيْنِۙ‏(56)\n\nHe shall say: “By God! thou hast almost caused me to perish!\nوَلَوْلَا نِعْمَةُ رَبِّىْ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِيْنَ‏(57)\n\nAnd had it not been the bounty of my Lord, certainly would I (too) have been (with thee) brought into (the Hell)\nاَفَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَيِّتِيْنَۙ‏(58)\n\nIs it then we die not (hereafter)?\nاِلَّا مَوْتَتَنَا الْاُوْلٰى وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‏(59)\n\nSave our first death; And we shall not be chastised?\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(60)\n\nVerily this is a great achievement.\nلِمِثْلِ هٰذَا فَلْيَعْمَلِ الْعٰمِلُوْنَ‏(61)\n\nFor the like of this should act every active one!\nاَذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ نُّزُلًا اَمْ شَجَرَةُ الزَّقُّوْمِ‏(62)\n\nIs this the better entertainment or the tree of Zaqqum?\nاِنَّا جَعَلْنٰهَا فِتْنَةً لِّلظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(63)\n\nVerily, We have made it a trial for the unjust.\nاِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِىْۤ اَصْلِ الْجَحِيْمِۙ‏(64)\n\nVerily, it is a tree that groweth in the bottom of the hell,\nطَلْعُهَا كَاَنَّهٗ رُءُوْسُ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ‏(65)\n\nIts produce is (ugly) as the heads of the satans.\nفَاِنَّهُمْ لَاٰكِلُوْنَ مِنْهَا فَمٰلِئُوْنَ مِنْهَا الْبُطُوْنَ ؕ‏(66)\n\nAnd verily they shall eat from it and fill (their) bellies with it.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا لَشَوْبًا مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍۚ‏(67)\n\nThen verily for them shall be to drink over it, a mixture in boiling water.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ مَرْجِعَهُمْ لَا۟اِلَى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(68)\n\nThen verily their return shall be unto the hell\nاِنَّهُمْ اَلْفَوْا اٰبَآءَهُمْ ضَآلِّيْنَۙ‏(69)\n\nVerily they found their fathers going astray,\nفَهُمْ عَلٰٓى اٰثٰرِهِمْ يُهْرَعُوْنَ‏(70)\n\nSo they in their footsteps did hasten on.\nوَلَقَدْ ضَلَّ قَبْلَهُمْ اَكْثَرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(71)\n\nAnd indeed went astray most of the ancients before them,\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا فِيْهِمْ مُّنْذِرِيْنَ‏(72)\n\nAnd indeed We did send among them warners.\nفَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَۙ‏(73)\n\nSee then how had been the end of those (already) warned,\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(74)\n\nSave the servants of God, the freed ones (from sinning).\nوَلَقَدْ نَادٰٮنَا نُوْحٌ فَلَنِعْمَ الْمُجِيْبُوْنَ  ۖ‏(75)\n\nAnd indeed did call on Us Noah, and (We are) the Most Excellent answerers (of prayer)\nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِ  ۖ‏(76)\n\nAnd We, delivered him and his followers from the great distress.\nوَجَعَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهٗ هُمُ الْبٰقِيْنَ  ۖ‏(77)\n\nAnd We made his progeny the survivors.\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَ  ۖ‏(78)\n\nAnd We did perpetuate for him (his praise) in the later generations.\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى نُوْحٍ فِى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(79)\n\nPeace be on Noah in all the worlds!\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(80)\n\nVerily thus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(81)\n\nVerily he was (one) of Our faithful servants.\nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(82)\n\nThen We drowned the others.\nوَاِنَّ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ لَاِبْرٰهِيْمَۘ‏(83)\n\nAnd verily of his persuasion was Abraham.\nاِذْ جَآءَ رَبَّهٗ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيْمٍ‏(84)\n\nWhen came he unto his Lord with a submissive heart,\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَاذَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۚ‏(85)\n\nWhen said he unto his father and his people: “What is it that ye worship?\nاَئِفْكًا اٰلِهَةً دُوْنَ اللّٰهِ تُرِيْدُوْنَؕ‏(86)\n\nIs it a falsehood - gods other than (the One True) God, desire ye?\nفَمَا ظَنُّكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(87)\n\nWhat then think ye about the Lord of the worlds?\nفَنَظَرَ نَظْرَةً فِى النُّجُوْمِۙ‏(88)\n\nThen glanced he, casting glance at the stars,\nفَقَالَ اِنِّىْ سَقِيْمٌ‏(89)\n\nThen said he: “Verily, sick I am (of your worshipping these)\nفَتَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(90)\n\nSo they turned away turning their backs.\nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اٰلِهَتِهِمْ فَقَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَۚ‏(91)\n\nThen he turned unto their gods secretly and said: “What! eat ye not?\nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(92)\n\nWhat aileth you that ye speak not?\nفَرَاغَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضَرْبًۢا بِالْيَمِيْنِ‏(93)\n\nThen he attacked them in secret, striking with his right hand\nفَاَقْبَلُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يَزِفُّوْنَ‏(94)\n\nThen came they (the worshippers) hastening unto him.\nقَالَ اَتَعْبُدُوْنَ مَا تَنْحِتُوْنَۙ‏(95)\n\nSaid he: “What! worship ye what ye (yourselves) hew out?\nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(96)\n\nAnd God hath created you and (also) what ye make (the idols)\nقَالُوا ابْنُوْا لَهٗ بُنْيَانًا فَاَلْقُوْهُ فِى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(97)\n\nSaid they: “Erect for him a building (furnace) and fling him in the flaming fire!\nفَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنٰهُمُ الْاَسْفَلِيْنَ‏(98)\n\nSo they desired a plot against him, but We brought them low.\nوَقَالَ اِنِّىْ ذَاهِبٌ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(99)\n\nAnd said he: “Verily, I am going unto my Lord, He will guide me;\nرَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(100)\n\nO’ my Lord! Grant me a righteous (son)!\nفَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِغُلٰمٍ حَلِيْمٍ‏(101)\n\nSo We gave him the glad tidings of a son extremely forbearing\nفَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعْىَ قَالَ يٰبُنَىَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى فِى الْمَنَامِ اَنِّىْۤ اَذْبَحُكَ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا تَرٰىؕ قَالَ يٰۤاَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(102)\n\nAnd when (the son) reached (the age of) working with him, said he: “O’ my son! verily I saw in a dream that I sacrifice thee: now what is thy view?” Said (the son)! “O’ father! Do thou what thou art bidden; If God willeth, thou wilt find me of the steadfast ones\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهٗ لِلْجَبِيْنِۚ‏(103)\n\nAnd when they both had surrendered (themselves) to the will of God and he (Abraham) threw him (the son) upon his forehead,\nوَنَادَيْنٰهُ اَنْ يّٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُۙ‏(104)\n\nAnd We called out unto him: “O’ Abraham!\nقَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّءْيَا  ۚ اِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(105)\n\nIndeed hast thou proved true the dream; Verily thus do We recompense the doers of good!\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلٰٓؤُا الْمُبِيْنُ‏(106)\n\nVerily, this is an open trial.\nوَفَدَيْنٰهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(107)\n\nAnd We ransomed him with a Great Sacrifice.\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۖ‏(108)\n\nAnd We shifted (this blessing) on him (who is from) among the generations (to come) in later times;\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‏(109)\n\nPeace be on Abraham.\nكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(110)\n\nThus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(111)\n\nVerily he was (one) of Our faithful servants.\nوَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِاِسْحٰقَ نَبِيًّا مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(112)\n\nAnd We gave him the glad tidings of Isaac, a prophet from among the righteous ones.\nوَبٰرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَعَلٰٓى اِسْحٰقَؕ وَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحْسِنٌ وَّظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهٖ مُبِيْنٌ‏(113)\n\nAnd bestowed We Our blessings on him and on Isaac: and on their progeny are the doers of good, and those (too) who are openly unjust to their own selves.\nوَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَۚ‏(114)\n\nAnd indeed conferred We Our favour on Moses and Aaron.\nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُمَا وَقَوْمَهُمَا مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِۚ‏(115)\n\nAnd We delivered them both and their people from the great distress\nوَنَصَرْنٰهُمْ فَكَانُوْا هُمُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَۚ‏(116)\n\nAnd We succoured them, so they were the triumphants.\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمَا الْكِتٰبَ الْمُسْتَبِيْنَۚ‏(117)\n\nAnd We gave them both the Book making things clear.\nوَهَدَيْنٰهُمَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَۚ‏(118)\n\nAnd We guided them both on the right way.\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِمَا فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(119)\n\nAnd We perpetuated their praise in the later generations,\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(120)\n\nPeace be on Moses and Aaron.\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(121)\n\nVerily, thus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهُمَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(122)\n\nVerily, they were both Our faithful servants,\nوَاِنَّ اِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(123)\n\nAnd verily, Elias was (one) of the apostles.\nاِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(124)\n\nWhen said he unto his people; “What! Guard ye not yourselves (against evil)?\nاَتَدْعُوْنَ بَعْلًا وَّتَذَرُوْنَ اَحْسَنَ الْخٰلِقِيْنَۙ‏(125)\n\nWhat! Call ye upon Ba’l and forsake the Best of the creators?\nاللّٰهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(126)\n\nGod, is your Lord and the Lord of your fathers of yore?\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(127)\n\nBut they belied him, so they shall certainly be brought (to account),\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(128)\n\nSave the servants of God, the freed ones (from sinning)\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(129)\n\nAnd We perpetuated his praise in the later generations,\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِلْ يَاسِيْنَ‏(130)\n\nPeace be on ‘Ilyasin’ (Elias).\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(131)\n\nVerily, thus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(132)\n\nVerily, he was (one) of Our faithful servants.\nوَاِنَّ لُوْطًا لَّمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(133)\n\nAnd verily Lot, was (one) of the apostles.\nاِذْ نَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(134)\n\nWhen We delivered him and his followers all.\nاِلَّا عَجُوْزًا فِى الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(135)\n\nSave an aged woman among those who tarried.\nثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(136)\n\nThen We destroyed the others.\nوَاِنَّكُمْ لَتَمُرُّوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ مُّصْبِحِيْنَۙ‏(137)\n\nAnd verily, ye pass by (their ruined dwellings) at morn,\nوَبِالَّيْلِؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(138)\n\nAnd at night; What! (even) then understand ye not?\nوَاِنَّ يُوْنُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(139)\n\nAnd verily Jonah was (one) of the apostles.\nاِذْ اَبَقَ اِلَى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِۙ‏(140)\n\nWhen he fled unto a ship fully laden,\nفَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُدْحَضِيْنَۚ‏(141)\n\nAnd they drew lots, and he was of those who were cast off.\nفَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوْتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌ‏(142)\n\nAnd the fish swallowed him while he was blamed.\nفَلَوْلَاۤ اَنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِيْنَۙ‏(143)\n\nSo if it were not that he was of those who glorify Us,\nلَلَبِثَ فِىْ بَطْنِهٖۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَۚ‏(144)\n\nHe would certainly have been detained in its belly to the Day (of Resurrection) when they shall be raised;\nفَنَبَذْنٰهُ بِالْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ سَقِيْمٌۚ‏(145)\n\nAnd We cast him forth on the naked shore and he was sick.\nوَاَنْۢبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّنْ يَّقْطِيْنٍۚ‏(146)\n\nAnd caused We to grow (to give shade) over him, a plant of gourd.\nوَاَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى مِائَةِ اَلْفٍ اَوْ يَزِيْدُوْنَۚ‏(147)\n\nAnd We sent him unto a hundred thousand (people) or (even) more were they.\nفَاٰمَنُوْا فَمَتَّعْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى حِيْنٍؕ‏(148)\n\nAnd believed they, so We gave them provision till a time.\nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَلِرَبِّكَ الْبَنَاتُ وَلَهُمُ الْبَنُوْنَۙ‏(149)\n\nThen ask them (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) Is it that thy Lord hath daughters, and they have sons?\nاَمْ خَلَقْنَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ اِنَاثًا وَّهُمْ شٰهِدُوْنَ‏(150)\n\nOr have We created the angels, females? and did they witness it?\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ مِّنْ اِفْكِهِمْ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(151)\n\nBeware! Verily it is of their own falsehood that they say:\nوَلَدَ اللّٰهُۙ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(152)\n\n(that) God hath begotten: And verily they utter a lie.\nاَصْطَفَى الْبَنَاتِ عَلَى الْبَنِيْنَؕ‏(153)\n\nHath he preferred daughters to sons?\nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(154)\n\nWhat hath happened to you? How judge ye?\nاَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَۚ‏(155)\n\nWhat! will ye not then reflect?\nاَمْ لَكُمْ سُلْطٰنٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(156)\n\nOr have ye any clear authority?\nفَاْتُوْا بِكِتٰبِكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(157)\n\nThen bring ye your book if ye be truthful.\nوَجَعَلُوْا بَيْنَهٗ وَبَيْنَ الْجِنَّةِ نَسَبًا ؕ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمَتِ الْجِنَّةُ اِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(158)\n\nAnd assign they between Him and the jinn a kinship, and indeed the jinn to know that they shall surely be brought up (to account on the Day of Judgment)\nسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۙ‏(159)\n\nHallowed is God far above from what they ascribe (unto Him),\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(160)\n\nBut (not so are) the servants, freed (from sinning)\nفَاِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(161)\n\nSo verily ye and what ye worship,\nمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ بِفٰتِنِيْنَۙ‏(162)\n\nYe can excite not (any one) against Him,\nاِلَّا مَنْ هُوَ صَالِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(163)\n\nExcept him who goes to Hell.\nوَمَا مِنَّاۤ اِلَّا لَهٗ مَقَامٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(164)\n\nAnd there is not (any one) of us, but for him is an assigned place,\nوَّاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الصَّآفُّوْنَۚ‏(165)\n\nAnd verily we are they who range ourselves in order.\nوَاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْمُسَبِّحُوْنَ‏(166)\n\nAnd verily we are they who celebrate His praise.\nوَاِنْ كَانُوْا لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(167)\n\nAnd certainly they used to say,\nلَوْ اَنَّ عِنْدَنَا ذِكْرًا مِّنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(168)\n\nHad we a reminder from those of yore,\nلَكُنَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(169)\n\nCertainly had we been the servants of God, sincerely devoted\nفَكَفَرُوْا بِهٖ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(170)\n\nThen disbelieved they with it, so, soon will they know.\nوَلَقَدْ سَبَقَتْ كَلِمَتُنَا لِعِبَادِنَا الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(171)\n\nAnd indeed Our word hath already gone forth about Our servants, the apostles:\nاِنَّهُمْ لَهُمُ الْمَنْصُوْرُوْنَ ‏(172)\n\nVerily they shall be the succoured ones.\nوَاِنَّ جُنْدَنَا لَهُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(173)\n\nAnd verily Our hosts, (only) they shall be the victorious.\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(174)\n\nSo turn thou away from them for a time,\nوَاَبْصِرْهُمْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(175)\n\nAnd (then) behold thou: for they too shall soon behold (their doom).\nاَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(176)\n\nWhat! would they then hasten on Our chastisement?\nفَاِذَا نَزَلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ فَسَآءَ صَبَاحُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(177)\n\nBut when it shall descend in their court, evil shall then be the morning of the warned ones.\nوَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(178)\n\nAnd turn thou away from them for a time,\nوَّاَبْصِرْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(179)\n\nAnd (then) behold thou, for they too shall soon see (their doom).\nسُبْحٰنَ رَبِّكَ رَبِّ الْعِزَّةِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۚ‏(180)\nSUBHAANA RABBEKA RABBIL I’ZZATE AMMAA YASEFOON.\nHallowed is thy Lord, the Lord of Majesty, far above from that which they ascribe (unto Him)\nوَسَلٰمٌ عَلَى الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۚ‏(181)\nWA SALAAMUN A’LAL MURSALEEN. \nAnd peace be upon the apostles.\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(182)\nWAL HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd all praise is God’s, the Lord of the worlds.",
  "merits": "There are 182 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the total number of Jinn and Shayateen that exist. The reciter of this Surah is protected from Shaitan and is safe from falling into disbelief and Shirk. His angels who record his deeds will testify for him on the Day of Judgement that he was from among those who believed in the Prophets of Allah (s.w.t.).\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that reciting Surah as-Saaffaat on every Friday keeps one safe from all types of calamities. His sustenance will increase and his life, wealth and children will be protected from the evil designs of Shaitan and the tyrant rulers of the time. If one dies soon after reciting this Surah, he will die the death of a martyr; he will be raised on the Day of Judgement together with the martyrs and will enter Jannah with them."
}
